  "summary": "Currently, I have been with Software Management, LLC in Louisville Kentucky for 8.5 years as a Software Developer.  My responsibilities include updates and new development in C# and Crystal Reports for our suite of Windows Forms apps, as well as maintaining and updating our ASP .NET web application and associated SQL databases, and more recently a newer version of the web app with technologies such as MVC, Bootstrap JS, Kendo UI, Entity Framework, javascript and jQuery as well as a SQL backend.  \n\nHighlights of my time here also include:\n* Developing and implementing a process that allows users to receive documents digitally from vendors and review, stamp and file said documents into our system\n* Multiple data imports and conversions for new and old customers into our SQL backend with both SQL scripts and custom C# applications\n* Helping new developers on the team understand our applications workflows, backend data structures and processes we use on a daily basis\n\nI graduated from Indiana University Southeast in May of 2011 with a Bachelor of Science Degree in Informatics with a cognate of Digital Media. I have an academic background in Information Technology and as well as experience with programming, database management, human computer interaction and project team management.\n\nI co-developed the STAIRS app while working at IUS and helped create databases for the application.  STAIRS is a form which incoming students fill out in order to attend informational sessions on their majors.\n\nWith the AME Group I developed an application in Access with VBA for a client as well as assisted with debugging and troubleshooting.  Co-developed a website portal in ASP.NET/VB.NET for another client and managed/updated various ASP.NET forms.  I also helped manage and maintain SQL and Access databases for our clients.\n\nSpecialties: ASP.NET MVC, Bootstrap, Kendo UI, C#, .NET, Javascript and jQuery, SQL and Microsoft SQL Server Management Studio, Microsoft SQL Server 2008, HTML, CSS, MVC, Microsoft Office Suite(Word, PowerPoint, Access, Excel), Microsoft and Mac operating systems, social sites such as Facebook, Twitter and Wordpress",
